<newsitem itemid="174334" id="root" date="1996-11-07" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: J. Bibby Year pre-tax rises 30 percent.</title>
<headline>J. Bibby Year pre-tax rises 30 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		16.9		   vs 12.1</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 7.5		    vs 5.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     42.8		   vs 32.9</p>
<p> Turnover		   785		    vs 736</p>
<p> Operating profit	 51.2		   vs 41.0</p>
<p> Interest		   8.3		    vs 8.1</p>
<p> Tax			  15.5		   vs 13.6</p>
<p> Attributable	     26.5		   vs 18.9</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 31, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Dec 10</p>
<p>NOTE - Diversified industrials company J. Bibby and Sons Plc said its strategy based on profitable growth from existing businesses and related acquisitions should enable it to show further progress in the year ahead.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
